## SQ-BLC-01
@group A
@commands Boot a new world; grep latest.log for `[biome-tuning]` and note the time from `biome_overrides.js` to the next KubeJS line
@pass `inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve (disk)`, no `override minecraft:overworld` lines; under 2 s; the world's `level.dat` has the tuned layout (`/locate biome` a tuned rare biome, e.g. one lifted by the rarity floor, finds one as before)
@fails `override ...` lines (a solve): the shipped file's key does not match the jar (seeded from `build/classes`, or jar rebuilt after seeding); re-seed with the jar's classes
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
shell grep -n "biome_overrides\|\[biome-tuning\]" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log | head -6 | cut -c1-200
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:mushroom_fields
waitlog (nearest minecraft:mushroom_fields|Could not find) 300
look under 2 s between the biome_overrides.js line and the next KubeJS line; the locate finds a rare biome as before
## SQ-BLC-02
@group A
@commands Delete `biome_layout_cache.json.gz`, boot; then `/reload`
@pass Boot: the `override` lines (a solve, about 10 s) and the file written again, byte-identical to the instance's copy (`cmp`); `/reload`: `(memory)`
@fails File not written: look for `could not write` in the messages; differs: the solve is not deterministic
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
shell test -s kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz && cmp kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz" && echo "cache rewritten, identical"
> reload
waitlog \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(memory\) 120
look own boot with srv/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz deleted first: the override lines (a solve, about 10 s) on the boot
## SQ-BLC-03
@group A
@commands Change one biome multiplier in `biome_config.json`, boot
@pass A solve with the new value and the file rewritten with a new key; restore the value, boot: solve again (the file holds one key), then `(disk)` on the boot after
@fails `(disk)` right after the edit: the key misses the config
@draft three boots with a biome_config.json edit and its restore between them (solve with the new key, solve again after the restore, then disk): a runner loop; per boot bootexpect the solve / (disk) line and a zcat key check of the cache file
@@text
@@text Results 2026-10-27 night: SQ-BLC-01 PASS (`(disk)` on every boot with the shipped file, 1.4 s; `/reload` `(memory)`); tuned-biome locate not run. SQ-BLC-02 PASS: file deleted -> solve (14.7 s) and the rewritten file byte-identical to the instance copy. SQ-BLC-03 PASS: badlands multiplier 1 -> 1.5 solved (13.6 s) and rewrote the file; restoring it solved again (combined with -02).
